imidating it's certainly much more  peaceful so I think res is another great  example despite the fact that it's  almost two decades  it's still a really good game that  translates very well to VR is it a  straight port or did they like Taylor  certain things to so it's another's head  tracking it's basically a straight port  there is one level that I haven't played  yet we're still waiting for the full  version I've only played the demo levels  that came with the headset full version  has a level that is not unrealistic for  this experience but even so I think  right now if you put res in VR in front  of me or the Dreamcast original I would  immediately play the VR version because  just being enveloped and this is like  your eyes drawn right feels like you're  in Tron and and again another game that  falls into that category is super hyper  cute simple puzzle game on its face you  know those Japanese TV shows where  people are on a moving platform and  there are walls coming at them with like  holes cut out and they have to like bend  their bodies to fit through right so  what you're doing is you're using a  cluster of cubes and you have to rotate  it to pass through a hole in the wall  for every hole you go through more cubes  are added on this is again much more  approachable then maybe even res which  is super approachable but it does  provide that sense of immersion in what  really amounts to like laser light shows  from the 80s remember your school photo  so they would have liked that weird  laser streaking in the background it's  exactly like that and you're just  floating through it the whole time  trying to solve these puzzles which gets  pretty tough I think this game could be  it could take advantage of VR a little  bit better in terms of the gameplay it  doesn't really do so much it's much more  about the atmosphere but again I think  for people who just want to get their  feet wet and give it a shot which might  be the thing that really helps sell VR  rather than the intense experiences I  think super hyper cube is going to do  that for a lot of people  alright those are our favorite  PlayStation VR games that we think you  were going to like which ones are you  interested in let us know in the  comments below for more PlayStation VR  coverage stay tuned to gamespot com  I
 

